WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
A window over the sea at Whitby.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.420
Two young women, two very different desks.

3
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:09.340
Mina writes in her journal
about the New Woman,

4
00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.480
who "will do the proposing herself".

5
00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:16.700
Later, beside Mina, things
pile up: a typewriter,

6
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.100
a railway timetable,
a stack of typescript.

7
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:23.110
Then her chair is pushed
back from a table of men,

8
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.080
and a door closes.

9
00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:29.990
So why does a woman who laughs at the
New Woman end up doing the men's work?

10
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:33.300
In this mission, you'll find out
what the New Woman stood for,

11
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:38.560
from 1894: education, paid
work, choice in marriage.

12
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.710
And you'll follow two
friends, Lucy and Mina,

13
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.100
to two very different fates.

14
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.810
Your mission: explain why
she does the men's work.
